<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dom Domingos of Warri</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dom Domingos was an Olu, or king, of the Itsekiri kingdom of Warri in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/niger-delta">Niger Delta</a> in the early 17th century. Raised as a Catholic under the influence of Portuguese missionaries, he spent several years in Portugal and around 1600 married a Portuguese woman. His reign marked the height of Portuguese religious and commercial influence at Warri.</p></div>
